    {
      "question": "q-32866",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "f0fe4e3e99530bf2cdf9ab3b9a0009349f2a60648ef759db145c7255b61d37dd",
      "new_sha256": "1a4d992bb557d8e8e15a1c01e6276f93bbd49e7547a950a6a05cd3e8fdb18c57",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "q-32866",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f\u2218u)^{\u2032}(t)={f}^{\u2032}(u(t)){u}^{\u2032}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(1-{u}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(12)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\,i-2u\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\,i-2u\\,j \\\\ {u}^{\u2032}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})=3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\u2218u)^{\u2032}(t) & ={f}^{\u2032}(u(t))\\cdot {u}^{\u2032}(t) \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(u(t))\\,i-2(u(t))\\,j)\\cdot {u}^{\u2032}(t) \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({t}^{3})\\,i-2({t}^{3})\\,j)\\cdot 3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{t}^{3}\\,i-6{t}^{5}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json",
          "file_sha256": "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"
        }
